        <ns3:IAO_0000116 xml:lang="en">Do not oversimplify the particulate environmental material subclasses with design patterns or similar. The materials have properties that their components do not - write full definitions including these where possible.</ns3:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EcoLexicon:sand</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <ns3:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">Particulate environmental material which is composed primarily of particles of sand with only minor proportions of other substances.</ns3:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">This definition is intentionally ambiguous to support the multiple thresholds set by different authorities. Some authorities consider as sands soil material that contains 85% or more sand; the percentage of silt plus 1.5 times the percentage of clay does not exceed 15. coarse sand (sable grossier) 25% or more very coarse and coarse sand, and less than 50% any other one grade of sand.</rdfs:comment>
